BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downtown Mystic Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:84b25dc48e9bfb13f9ce1fcdc754@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Our Original Ghost Walk takes travelers through the historic d
 owntown Mystic landscape crossing the bascule bridge between both sides of
  the Mystic River\, guests will become immersed in the dark\, sordid and s
 upernatural history of New England’s famous seafaring village. From 17th
  century strife of colonial life amidst the Pequot Wars and the King Phill
 ip’s war to mysterious turn of the century murders\, Mystic’s history 
 was founded in darkness. As the centuries grew\, lost seafarers\, creepy c
 ryptids\, and scandalous happenings took place in our quaint seaside commu
 nity.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Liberty Pole Square\, East Main Street\, Holmes Street\, Mystic C
 T\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Style & Substance: A Special Exhibit
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:3ba4db603bc6c3aba28a9458e2e5@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This Special Exhibit at the Kate showcases some of Katharine H
 epburn's most stunning gowns and highlights the depth of intention behind 
 them. Kate worked with costumes designers to ensure that the right cuts an
 d silhouettes were used to flatter her tall\, athletic frame\; she knew th
 at when it comes to a life in the spotlight\, image is everything. Explore
  the way she crafted her unique look and became a lasting style icon.\n\nS
 ource: https://ctvisit.com/events/style-substance-special-exhibit
LOCATION:Katharine Hepburn Cultural Arts Center\, 300 Main Street\, Old Sa
 ybrook CT\, 06475
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/style-substance-special-exhibit
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Pronounced Ah-Beetz" Exhibit
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:a17a239c2736d19714d63aeedc21@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:From Frank Pepe’s original hat to celebrity-signed pizza box
 es (including Gwyneth Paltrow and Yogi Berra!)\, if you love the crust\, t
 he crunch and the char of New Haven apizza\, or simply have strong views o
 n what comprises a good pie\, you’ll find something to feed your persona
 l pizza passion in the exhibit “Pronounced Ah-Beetz\,” at the New Have
 n Museum (NHM)\, which is on view through October 2027.\n\nSource: https:/
 /ctvisit.com/events/pronounced-ah-beetz-exhibit
LOCATION:New Haven Museum\, 114 Whitney Avenue\, New Haven CT\, 06512
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/pronounced-ah-beetz-exhibit
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independence Revisited: Sharon in 1776\, 1876 & 1976
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:23ea6076988d4b14f8723179c35d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:By examining Sharon through the lens of three pivotal mileston
 es—1776\, 1876\, and 1976—the exhibition explores how broader national
  transformations informed the local experience. Independence Revisited beg
 ins with a study of 18th-century life and follows the town’s physical\, 
 social\, and political trajectory\, ultimately investigating how Sharon ch
 ose to commemorate\, interpret\, or overlook its revolutionary heritage du
 ring these defining moments in American history.\n\nSource: https://ctvisi
 t.com/events/independence-revisited-sharon-1776-1876-1976
LOCATION:Sharon Historical Society & Museum\, 18 Main Street\, Sharon CT\,
  06069
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/independence-revisited-sharon-1776-1876-197
 6
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:America250: THE REAL REVOLUTION
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271202
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:d496508c04ff23629e29f741202e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:A mother with sons on opposing side of a life-changing conflic
 t. Enslaved men risking their lives for freedom. A woman posing as a man i
 n the fight for liberty. These are just a few of the people who are explor
 ed in The Real Revolution\, Westport Museum’s 2026 exhibit honoring the 
 250th anniversary of the founding of the nation. The exhibit delves into t
 he untold stories of the people who lived through the life-changing events
  of war and nation building. The exhibition includes an interactive playro
 om for kids\, and a tavern room in which special events will be held.\n\nS
 ource: https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
LOCATION:Westport Museum For History And Culture\, 25 Avery Place\, Westpo
 rt CT\, 06880
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Words on Wood Party
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:30141fc642694de689a557083d0e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Choose a Words on Wood design or design your own. We will prep
 are all of your materials and when you arrive\, we will walk you through t
 he process\, step by step\, to create your masterpiece. Make sure to check
  out the shops offered at Wallingford Marketplace while you’re here! You
 ’re invited to join us early to shop & take photos in the photo booth. B
 everages – wine\, beer\, cider & soft drinks – are available to purcha
 se at the bar. Outside food is welcome\, but outside beverages are not per
 mitted. Mention CTVisit for a free drink at The Woodshed Bar during the pa
 rty.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/words-wood-party-1
LOCATION:The Wallingford Marketplace at Words on Wood\, 144 CENTER STREET
 \, WALLINGFORD CT\, 06492
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/words-wood-party-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norwich Stories of the American Revolution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:c5d13aef0c36e1820a30a1a8eed9@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Norwich\, Connecticut was a center of Revolutionary activity i
 n Eastern Connecticut. From bands of Sons of Liberty to dedicated soldiers
  of all backgrounds\, the city produced scores of men and women who served
  in all capacities. From humble militiamen to a Signer of the Declaration 
 of Independence\, come and learn the lesser-known stories of these valiant
  Patriots as well as the story of America’s most infamous traitor\, Bene
 dict Arnold.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-america
 n-revolution
LOCATION:Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sharks Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:e900bdd06c9878548021b8ca7c6d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:People have been fascinated by sharks for as long as we have e
 xplored the ocean\, and now the Connecticut Science Center is bringing tha
 t fascination to life in the limited-time exhibition\, Sharks. This immers
 ive experience brings you face-to-face with some of the ocean’s most fas
 cinating predators through full-scale shark models\, interactive experienc
 es\, underwater environments\, ancient fossils\, immersive media\, and —
  of course — a lot of teeth.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/shark
 s-exhibition
LOCATION:Connecticut Science Center\, 250 Columbus Boulevard\, Hartford CT
 \, 06103
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/sharks-exhibition
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fairfield in 1776: Revolution & Resilience Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260514
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTSTAMP:20261106T174854Z
UID:a01a280969953b149edaf2f5aaf3@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:2026 marks the 250th anniversary of the Declaration of Indepen
 dence. Step into colonial Fairfield and learn what the town was like in th
 e years leading up to 1776. The exhibition will explore the many facets of
  the people who made up the Fairfield community in 1776\, from their ethni
 c and religious backgrounds and socio-economic status to the languages the
 y spoke. Discover who in the colonial community held power at the signing 
 of the Declaration of Independence–and who didn’t.\n\nSource: https://
 ctvisit.com/events/fairfield-1776-revolution-resilience-exhibition
LOCATION:Fairfield Museum & History Center\, 370 Beach Rd\, Fairfield\, CT
 \, 06824\, Fairfield CT\, 06824
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/fairfield-1776-revolution-resilience-exhibi
 tion
END:VEVENT
